  "reason": "The two completed experiments show that image-only (config_019, acc=0.208) performs very poorly, while multimodal with scvi_n200 + resnet50 (config_038, acc=0.536) performs much better. The critical uncertainty is whether the image modality is genuinely contributing to the 0.536 result or whether the performance is driven almost entirely by the RNA encoder. Config_022 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_038—the only difference is the removal of the image branch. If RNA alone approaches 0.536, the image is not adding value and the search should focus on RNA encoder choice and multiprofile aggregation. If RNA alone is substantially lower, the image is a meaningful contributor and subsequent experiments should explore image encoders and fusion strategies. This is the highest-information experiment under the limited budget because it resolves the fundamental question of whether multimodality is warranted before investing further experiments in image-side or fusion-side design choices."
}

